# structural findings per Debian source, for humans (not read by tools)
inetutils: its tools (telnet, ping, syslogd ...) are alternatives in Debian and would overlap openSUSE's own packages; skipped
distro-info: needs distro-info-data at runtime (was blocklisted, now packaged); the Makefile honours $VENDOR, hence `unset VENDOR` in %debian_env
python3-*: ${python3:Depends} substvars are dropped, so python runtime dependencies are missing from the rpm (dh_python3 computes them at Debian build time)
netcat: update-alternatives from postinst is ignored, so /usr/bin/nc is not provided
dh-elpa: Slowroll's mailutils wants guile = 3.0.9 while 3.0.11 is shipped; worked around with `Ignore: emacs:mailutils` in data/prjconf
